title One page, two repositories
prompt Keaton asked to audit the roster for blind classes; to silo an email he sent a vegan-aligned VC and adapt it into a new universal foundations writing; to rewrite the root README for both the seed and the personal repo, fixing links that break under the seed scrub; and to check whether the recursion loops are ready to restart.
think Audited the roster empirically rather than by reasoning about it -- six candidate blind classes, each measured. Case collisions 0, largest blob 2.8 MB, rule twins 39/40 with none claiming an absent twin, submodules declared cleanly. Four healthy, two blind.
think Blind class one is the seed projection. The seed is an ALLOWLIST built from template-manifest.bron, and `gratitude` and `vendor` are filtered out of it explicitly, so every README link into gratitude dies in the public repo. Measured 867 dead links across living shipped documents, 19 in the front door.
think The reason no guard caught it is worth naming exactly: `tracked_link` asks "is this in the repository," which is the right question for the field and the wrong question for the seed. A guard proves a property of the repository it runs in, and this tree ships two.
think Blind class two came out of a zero-byte sweep: two tracked files at 0 bytes, one a session log indexed in session-logs/README.md. Vacuous truth is the shape -- a check phrased as "nothing here is wrong" is satisfied perfectly by a file with nothing in it.
think Before siloing the letter I checked remote visibility, because the letter carries family financial details and a friend's venture. All three remotes read PUBLIC. That changed the placement decision entirely and surfaced %162.
think The seed's whole depersonalisation argument -- withhold the signature so the anonymous seed cannot be linked to the maintainer -- assumes the field is private. It is not. Content matching links the two repositories in one search, so the unsigned commit buys nothing it was meant to buy.
think Placed the letter in `letters/`, untracked by the `.gitignore` allowlist default, rather than in a seed-withheld-but-tracked room like `twilight/`. Seed-withholding is only privacy while the field is private.
think Siloed the letter per SILO_TECHNIQUE: kept the transferable truths, left every proper noun, brand, and figure at the door. Verified by grepping the result for thirty source terms -- one hit, and it was "slogan" containing "logan".
think The strongest thing the crossing found is a genuine convergence rather than a metaphor: a farm that makes its own fertility and a program that declares every allocation are the same discipline -- a system that renews itself from within needs no input it cannot account for. And a certification is a witness for a farm; both are worth exactly the rigour of their check.
think Wrote the README seed-safe by construction rather than by sweep: a withheld room is named in prose with nothing to click. That is the only shape that reads correctly in both repositories at once, and it is what makes the gratitude paragraph work without a single link into `gratitude/`.
obs Gated the new guard on a NAMED front door of four documents rather than a discovered set. A guard whose enforced set grows by itself reds on work it never agreed to cover, and the other 848 want a rewrite per document rather than a repoint -- so they ratchet under a ceiling that only falls.
obs Removed the SEED_LINK_CEILING environment override after writing it. A ceiling with a flag beside it is a habit; the control proves both sides by planting 849 dead links against 848 instead. SEED_LINK_MANIFEST stays, because the pen genuinely needs its own manifest -- that is a fixture input, not a gate bypass.
obs The scan agreed with an independent Python measurement on every field before I trusted it -- 848 after the README repair, 867 before, 198 in testimony. Two implementations reaching the same number is worth more than one implementation reading confidently.
obs REDS crossed its 24,576-byte bound twice this round; rows %157-%158 and then %159 folded to `crux/archive/` with doorway lines, and the headline was carried to 162. The monotone spine reads 1..162 with no gaps.
obs Booked %162 as an OPEN GATE rather than repairing it. All three resolutions are Keaton's word and two touch published history, so it is surfaced like a gate under Standfast rather than routed around.
