recommend check-in (Keaton) -- %162 is the gate and it is the real one: the depersonalisation protects a field that is already public, so the unsigned seed commit buys nothing while the field tracks a resume, a personal ontology, a cover letter, and the poems. Three resolutions, all yours, two touching published history. The loops are otherwise ready to restart. The expanded-prompts question has a measurement: 2 tracked files against expanding-prompts' 584, so unifying is nearly free -- yet it is a room removal, so it wants a cairn and your word.
